      "IPS -- An intrusion prevention system (IPS) monitors incoming and outgoing traffic looking for malware, network attack signatures, and more. If it recognizes a threat, it can immediately stop it.",
    summary:
      "IPS — INTRUSION PREVENTION SYSTEM\n\nAn IPS (Intrusion Prevention System) is a network security technology that monitors incoming and outgoing traffic in real time, identifies malicious patterns and attack signatures, and automatically stops threats before they can cause damage.\n\nKey characteristics of an IPS:\n- Software-based detection: uses signature databases, anomaly detection, and heuristics to identify known and emerging threats\n- Real-time analysis: inspects traffic as it flows through the network — not after the fact\n- Active prevention: when a threat is identified, the IPS can automatically drop the packet, block the connection, or alert the administrator\n- Monitors both directions: inspects inbound AND outbound traffic — catching threats entering the network and suspicious activity leaving it\n- Identifies fast-spreading threats: particularly effective against malware, worms, and exploit attempts that spread rapidly across a network\n\nIPS vs IDS vs Firewall:\n- IDS (Intrusion Detection System): monitors and alerts — does NOT block. Passive.\n- IPS (Intrusion Prevention System): monitors, detects, AND blocks automatically. Active.\n- Firewall: filters traffic based on static rules (IP, port, protocol). Does not analyse traffic content for attack signatures.\n- ACL: a router/switch rule set filtering by IP address or application — no threat intelligence.\n\nIPS deployment:\n- Placed inline in the network path — all traffic passes through it\n- Can be a dedicated hardware appliance, a virtual appliance, or software on a security device\n- Often combined with IDS functionality in modern security platforms (IDPS)\n\n💡 Analogy: An IPS is like a security guard who not only watches the CCTV (IDS) but also physically stops anyone matching a threat profile from entering the building — automatically, in real time, without waiting to be told.",
